      "real1": "The 2022 report disclosed 19 full-time Hong Kong staff, including directors, and an established complaint-handling procedure. It provides the background for this case: small teams also need to organise complaint handling.",
      "real2Title": "Cinda: the stages a complaint goes through",
      "real2": "Its public process covers receipt, acknowledgement, investigation, a final response and further feedback. Use it to see the overall sequence, then decide where this SOP should start and end.",
      "real3Title": "SFC appendix: what to check in the draft",
      "real3": "The appendix to circular 22EC30 specifies acknowledgement within seven days of receipt and a final response within two months, along with identification, escalation and record-keeping requirements. Use it to check for incorrect deadlines, missing escalation steps and missing follow-up records.",
      "sourceUseTitle": "How to give the sources to the AI",
      "sourceUse": "The learner pack includes Public Source Notes (01-public-source-notes.md). After creating the Grok project, attach the notes to the coach chat so the AI can use them when clarifying the sources. When you move to a fresh chat to write the SOP, also supply the materials listed in the prompt.",
      "fictionLabel": "Classroom scenario",
      "fictionTitle": "Harbour Practice Securities",
      "fictionText": "Imagine a 25-person Hong Kong securities broker that needs a procedure for new operations staff. The firm, clients and business materials are fictional; the role assignments below are part of the exercise.",
      "rolesTitle": "Meet the two roles",
      "roleHead1": "Role",
      "roleHead2": "Meaning",
      "roleHead3": "Responsibilities in this case",
      "opsMeaning": "Operations staff; Ops is short for Operations",
      "opsRole": "Receive and log complaints, collect information, pass the case on and keep tracking its status and deadlines.",
      "officerMeaning": "The person responsible for handling complaints",
      "officerRole": "Explicitly accept the handoff, assign the work, arrange the investigation and coordinate further handling.",
      "roleExample": "For example, a complaint arrives in the customer-service inbox. Operations staff log it and send it to the Complaints Officer. The handoff is complete only after an explicit reply accepting it, with the receiving person and time recorded. The complaint may still be unresolved, so operations staff continue tracking it.",
      "scopeTitle": "Where this SOP ends",
      "scopeText": "Cover receipt through explicit acceptance by the Complaints Officer, and assign continued status and deadline tracking to operations staff. Full investigation, compensation decisions, final client letters and final archiving belong to the later process.",
      "deadlineTitle": "When to acknowledge receipt to the client",
      "deadlineText": "The fictional firm aims to acknowledge receipt to the client within two business days; the supplied SFC source says within seven days of receipt. Apply the earlier deadline. This is the acknowledgement sent to the client; the Complaints Officer’s internal reply accepting the case is a separate action.",
      "s3": "3. Add the coach in Grok",
      "s3Intro": "Add the skill, create a project and supply the sources. We will call the conversation that uses the skill to clarify your needs and generate the prompt “coach chat A”.",
      "setup1Title": "Upload the skill",
      "setup1": "Tools → Skills → New skill → Upload skill file. Select SKILL.md inside the learner pack’s skills folder; if a ZIP is required, compress that skill’s folder and upload it.",
      "setup2Title": "Create a project",
      "setup2": "Name the project “My SOP Prompt”.",
      "setup3Title": "Attach the public source notes",
      "setup3": "Open a new chat in the project and use + beside the message box to upload 01-public-source-notes.md. These notes summarise the three public sources for the conversation that follows.",
      "setup4Title": "Select the skill and start coach chat A",
      "setup4": "Use + beside the message box → Skills → hk-sop-prompt-coach, then send the opening request from the next section. It should ask questions to clarify your needs. If it immediately produces an SOP, check that the skill is selected for this chat.",
      "s4": "4. Walk through the conversation",
      "s4Intro": "Complete the first five steps in coach chat A: describe your needs, answer questions, correct and confirm the brief, then receive a prompt. In step six, take it to fresh chat B to write the SOP. In step seven, bring a specific issue back to A. Each card says where its content belongs.",
      "where1": "Where to use it: coach chat A. Send the opening request below, then wait for the AI’s questions.",
      "where2": "Where to use it: stay in coach chat A. Use the company background and additional answers below to respond to the questions the AI actually asks.",
